# N-SQL Prototype Grammar (Core Subset)

This document defines the **minimal N-SQL grammar subset** implemented in `law-n-sql-core`.

## 1. Query Shape

```ebnf
query           = select_clause, from_clause, [ where_clause ], [ ";" ] ;
select_clause   = "SELECT", column_list ;
from_clause     = "FROM", identifier ;
where_clause    = "WHERE", condition_expr ;

column_list     = "*"
                | column_name, { ",", column_name } ;

column_name     = identifier ;

condition_expr  = condition_term, { "AND", condition_term } ;

condition_term  = comparison
                | in_expression ;

comparison      = identifier, comparator, value ;

in_expression   = identifier, "IN", "(", value, { ",", value }, ")" ;

comparator      = "=" | "!=" | "<" | "<=" | ">" | ">=" ;

identifier      = letter, { letter | digit | "_" | "." } ;

value           = string_literal
                | numeric_literal ;

string_literal  = "'", { any_char_except_quote }, "'" ;
numeric_literal = digit, { digit | "." } ;
